Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 17:49:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 25/25] discovery: wake a 4G camera without needless waits

- The confirmation of a map or relay connection (C2R_CFM) is sent five times 500 ms apart, and
  the connection waited for all five: 2 s between the camera's answer and the login. The first
  copy goes out now and the repeats in the background.
- A cellular camera, behind its operator's NAT, is reached through the relay, so the relay no
  longer starts 500 ms late there (the map still races it).
- Right after a camera has gone to sleep the Reolink server can answer a registration with
  "wait" (R2C_T) for the whole 15 s before it is given up, while a fresh registration is
  answered in about 3 s. A second registration with its own client id now starts 5 s after the
  first and the first answer wins.
---
 crates/core/src/bc_protocol.rs                | 42 ++++++++++++-
 .../src/bc_protocol/connection/discovery.rs   | 63 ++++++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 95 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

